# Boots a fresh profile as boot.b3t does, pairing the game's frame with the
# native view's (`capture screen-<kind>`) on each kind of screen it passes:
# the boot logos, the intro movie, the title and the first-run prompts. The
# first of three scripts that go through every kind of screen RB3 shows;
# render_screens_menus.b3t and render_screens_song.b3t go on from here.
#   python tools/band3ctl.py launch --fresh -- --renderer=emulated --native_view_record_targets=true --test_random_seed=21 --async_shader_compilation=false
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/render_screens_boot.b3t
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/render_screens_menus.b3t
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/render_screens_song.b3t
# Launch with --fresh: the prompts are a first boot's, and the songs the later
# scripts pick are where a fresh profile's music library has them. Even/odd
# rendering stays on, as the game ships, so the menus' captures are post
# frames composed with the world frame before them where RB3 draws by turns.
# Captures are under screenshots/ next to the exe: <name>.png the game's,
# <name>.cap the native view's capture, <name>.gpu.png its GPU drawing.
# After each capture `screenshot <name>-again` is the window's picture a
# command later (the emulated GPU's under the launch above, the native
# renderer's with --renderer=native): what moved by itself meanwhile, which
# tools/pairs.py --cross leaves out when it sets a run without the emulated
# GPU against this one (docs/native-renderer.md, Render checks). The render
# scripts below all take one.

# The boot logos: a Bink movie RB3's splash thread draws into a texture
# (TexMovie) and shows on a mesh, while the main thread loads. The frame count
# stands still meanwhile (it counts the main thread's frames), so this waits
# by the clock, for a logo to be up.
sleep 2s
capture screen-boot-logos
screenshot screen-boot-logos-again
# the intro movie, a movie screen of its own
wait screen=intro_movie_screen timeout=180s
sleep 4s
capture screen-intro-movie
screenshot screen-intro-movie-again
# the title (press start), over the city
wait screen=splash_screen timeout=120s
sleep 2s
capture screen-title
screenshot screen-title-again
press start until screen=first_time_calibration timeout=30s
sleep 1s
capture screen-calibration-prompt
screenshot screen-calibration-prompt-again
# Continue, not Calibrate System
press down
press green
# the dx_ screens are Rock Band 3 Deluxe's
wait screen=dx_welcome_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1s
capture screen-dx-welcome
screenshot screen-dx-welcome-again
# Let's Rock!
press green until screen=hint_rb3_welcome_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1s
capture screen-rb3-welcome
screenshot screen-rb3-welcome-again
